; Part of millgui. MIT licence, see millgui/LICENSE.
; CAL spindle nose (millgui CAL > SPINDLE NOSE). No arguments. With the
; spindle empty (T0), brings the bare spindle nose down onto the tool
; setter at the G30 position and measures how far below machine Z 0 it
; trips: that distance becomes the spindle zero height #3010, the
; reference tool_touch_off measures tool lengths from. Sets the setter max
; Z travel #3007 = 1.001 x #3010 and #1009 = the trip Z (program
; coordinates, no tool offset), and reports z_minus_probed_position,
; spindle_zero_height_3010 and z_max_travel_3007 (millgui saves the last
; two as new defaults). The trip height is taken from the G30 Z and the
; probed travel below it, as in tool_touch_off.
; In diameter offset mode #3012 = 1 the nose touches off centre by half
; the nose diameter, in direction #3013, so the setter meets the nose face
; and not the taper bore. The nose diameter comes from the INI file,
; [TOOL_SETTER]SPINDLE_NOSE_DIAMETER, readable only with [RS274NGC]
; INI_VARS = 1; without it diameter offset mode aborts. Motion and checks
; as tool_touch_off (o<millgui_setter_ready>, o<millgui_setter_touch>);
; feed override off during the run, modal state as it was afterwards.
; Unlike Probe Basic's version this macro sets no HAL latch: a machine
; that tracks "nose reference valid since homing" in HAL sets it from
; its own wrapper or GUI after this macro succeeds.
o<probe_spindle_nose> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_spindle_nose> return
o10 endif
o100 if [#5400 NE 0]
    (ABORT, Unload the spindle with T0 before measuring the spindle nose)
o100 endif
o<millgui_setter_ready> call
#<nose_d> = 0
o110 if [EXISTS[#<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]SPINDLE_NOSE_DIAMETER>]]
    #<nose_d> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]SPINDLE_NOSE_DIAMETER>
o110 endif
o120 if [[#3012 EQ 1] AND [#<nose_d> LE 0]]
    (ABORT, Diameter offset mode needs TOOL_SETTER SPINDLE_NOSE_DIAMETER in the INI file and INI_VARS on)
o120 endif

M5
M73
M50 P0
o<millgui_setter_touch> call [#<nose_d> / 2]
#<height> = [0 - #<_value>]
o200 if [#<height> LE 0]
    (ABORT, The spindle nose tripped the setter above machine Z 0)
o200 endif
#3010 = #<height>
#3007 = [1.001 * #<height>]
#1009 = #<_millgui_setter_trip>
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"z_minus_probed_position"}.setValue{#1009}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"spindle_zero_height_3010"}.setValue{#3010}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"z_max_travel_3007"}.setValue{#3007}])
o<probe_spindle_nose> endsub
M2
